ate"><addressbook><name>SATO, TATSUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIN-ETSU HANDOTAI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIN-ETSU QUARTZ PRODUCTS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOETA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IGARASHI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAWA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO TATSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SOETA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IGARASHI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAWA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, TATSUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOETA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The inner surface of a quartz glass crucible is crystallized, without adding any impurity, during the period in which a silicon single crystal is pulled up, whereby the deterioration of the inner surface of the crucible can be inhibited while preventing any impurity causative of crystal defects from coming into the single crystal. This crucible is effective in heightening the degree of conversion into a single crystal and is suitable for improving crucible productivity and the quality of silicon single crystals. The crucible is characterized by comprising a crucible base (3) which is a translucent quartz glass layer and a synthetic quartz glass layer (4) formed on the inner wall of the base (3) and by having been constituted so that that part of the inner crucible surface which is surrounded by a brown ring is evenly crystallized during the period in which a silicon single crystal is pulled up.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La surface intérieure d'un creuset en verre de quartz est cristallisée, sans ajout d'impuretés, pendant la période de croissance d'un monocristal de silicium, ce qui permet d'inhiber une détérioration de la surface intérieure du creuset tout en empêchant la pénétration dans le monocristal d'impuretés entraînant des défauts de cristal. Ce creuset sert à élever efficacement le degré de transformation en monocristal, et convient pour améliorer la productivité du creuset et la qualité de monocristaux de silicium. Le creuset est caractérisé par le fait qu'il comporte une base (3) de creuset constituée d'une couche de verre de quartz vitreux et une couche (4) de verre de quartz synthétique formée sur la paroi intérieure de la base (3); et qu'il est constitué de telle sorte que la partie de la surface intérieure du creuset qui est entourée par un anneau brun est cristallisée de façon uniforme pendant la période de croissance d'un monocristal de silicium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>